I don't know what the problem is, though here are some of the most common
mistakes I've made in my forays into dgamelaunching:

 * didn't make inprogress dir
 * incorrect permissions somewhere in the chroot (dgl drops privs so 
   running it as root may not be sufficient, depending)
 * missing entire directory somewhere in chroot
 * typo in config file

My recommendation is to run dgl as root under strace and see what you see
going on. To get a permanent blank screen seems a little weird to me...
I don't think I've seen that specific symptom before. Have you tried
running nethack from within the chroot as dgl would be running it? (so

 bash% chroot /path/to/chroot /usr/games/nethack 

or something similar depending on your system's configuration) That might
provide some information...

